      "message": "Robustness (P3): getattr(type(user), key).property raises AttributeError for any key that passes hasattr(user, key) but is not an SQLAlchemy-instrumented attribute. Probed: is_active/is_authenticated/is_anonymous (properties) and get_id/verify_password (bound functions) -\u003e AttributeError -\u003e unhandled 500; PATCH /users (users.py:182) forwards arbitrary JSON keys (admin-only endpoint; in-repo callers send only real columns today, so no current trigger). For read-only properties setattr already raised pre-patch (same 500 class), but for plain functions/attrs (e.g. get_id) setattr previously succeeded as a harmless shadow and now 500s. Suggest guarding the access before .property:\n    attr \u003d getattr(type(user), key, None)\n    prop \u003d getattr(attr, \"property\", None)\n    if value is not None and isinstance(prop, ColumnProperty) and type(prop.columns[0].type) is DateTime and not isinstance(value, datetime):\n        value \u003d parse_datetime(value)\nThis also makes the intent explicit (the roles relationship is only safe today because getattr(prop, \"columns\", None) happens to be None).",
